# سوق ميثلون Standards

## Product identity

- The official Arabic product name is `سوق ميثلون`.
- Never use the spelling `سوق مي&#1578;لون` or any alternative spelling.
- The product is an Arabic-first RTL cleaning-products ecommerce PWA for Palestinian customers.
- Currency is displayed using `₪`.
- Preserve accurate Arabic language and RTL layout.

## Engineering

- Write production-quality, secure, scalable, testable, and maintainable code.
- Follow the existing architecture and appropriate design patterns.
- Maintain separation of concerns and explicit feature boundaries.
- Prefer small focused modules and composition.
- Avoid overengineering, speculative abstractions, duplicated logic, and unnecessary dependencies.
- Do not modify unrelated files or behavior.
- Do not leave dead code, debug output, unexplained suppressions, or unnecessary TO&#68;O items.

## Comments and docstrings

- Do not add long comments, explanatory docstrings, or large documentation blocks inside source code.
- Prefer clear naming and clean structure.
- Add a short comment only for a non-obvious architectural decision, security constraint, business rule, or browser workaround.
- Do not generate verbose documentation unless explicitly requested.

## Security

- Treat browser input, URLs, cookies, local storage, API data, and uploads as untrusted.
- Validate data at trust boundaries.
- Keep authorization, pricing, discounts, stock, and business rules authoritative on the server.
- Never expose secrets or privileged credentials to client code.
- Never commit credentials, tokens, or real environment values.
- Never use unsafe HTML rendering.
- Apply least privilege.
- Do not weaken security to make tests pass.
- Never connect to or mutate production services without explicit authorization.

## UI and accessibility

- Preserve Arabic RTL behavior at every breakpoint.
- Use mobile-first responsive design.
- Desktop layouts must be intentionally designed.
- Follow the approved visual reference and design tokens.
- Use semantic HTML, accessible names, visible focus indicators, keyboard support, and WCAG AA contrast.
- Use minimum 44 × 44 CSS pixel touch targets.
- Handle loading, empty, error, unavailable, unauthorized, and offline states.
- Avoid excessive cards, pills, shadows, gradients, animation, and AI-generated decorative styling.
- Do not use emoji as interface icons.
- Do not invent ratings, reviews, discounts, stock, sizes, product claims, or customer counts.

## Next.js and React

- Use React Server Components by default.
- Use client components only for browser APIs, local interactions, or client state.
- Keep business logic out of presentational components.
- Avoid unnecessary effects and duplicated state.
- Keep server-only modules out of client bundles.
- Use framework-recommended routing, metadata, fonts, images, and caching.
- Never cache dynamic prices or stock in a way that can display stale authoritative data.

## Data architecture

- Access product data through repository or service boundaries.
- Do not couple pages directly to database clients or mock arrays.
- Keep future authoritative pricing and calculations server-side.
- Validate restored client state before using it.
- Design future schema changes to be reversible and safe.

## Verification

- Add focused tests for changed behavior.
- Test user outcomes instead of implementation details.
- Include RTL, accessibility, responsive, error, and security-relevant cases.
- Run formatting, linting, type checking, tests, and production build before completion.
- Never claim a check passed if it failed or was not executed.
- Report commands, results, changed files, and remaining risks.
